menuconfig SPARKLINK
	bool "SparkLink (NearLink) subsystem support"
	depends on RUST
	depends on NET
	select CONFIGFS_FS
	select CRYPTO
	select CRYPTO_AES
	select CRYPTO_CMAC
	select CRYPTO_ECDH
	help
	  SparkLink (also known as NearLink / 星闪) is a short-range wireless
	  communication technology designed for low-latency, low-power, and
	  high-reliability scenarios including smart terminals, smart home,
	  smart vehicles, and industrial IoT.

	  This option enables the SparkLink protocol stack, providing:
	    - SCI (SparkLink Controller Interface) device management
	    - SLE (Synchronous Low Energy) air interface support
	    - Native discovery, physical links and application channels
	    - Limited per-Session security mechanism; full Pair/install still pending

	  Say Y here to compile SparkLink support into the kernel or say M
	  to compile it as a module.

if SPARKLINK

config SPARKLINK_GENL
	bool "SparkLink Generic Netlink interface"
	depends on NET
	help
	  Adds read-only registry count and software version queries to the
	  "sparklink" Generic Netlink family. It does not select a controller,
	  submit commands or publish controller events. Identity-bound Native
	  APIs remain the controller management and observation path.

	  If unsure, say N.

source "drivers/sparklink/Kconfig"

endif # SPARKLINK
